WEBVTT

00:03:28.246 --> 00:03:30.706
which would give a total of 36.

00:03:30.915 --> 00:03:34.001
That eliminates 39 and 42.

00:03:34.252 --> 00:03:37.964
With 36, 
if we had 3 cells in each chamber,

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:42.927
each side of the upper level would already
have 9 of its 11 cells,

00:03:42.927 --> 00:03:46.180
meaning we’d have to leave empty chambers
on the lower level.

00:03:46.555 --> 00:03:48.975
So 36 is also out.

00:03:49.392 --> 00:03:50.768
What about 33?

00:03:50.977 --> 00:03:53.813
We know we don’t want any sides 
with all 3′s,

00:03:53.813 --> 00:03:57.566
so we can place 2′s at opposite
corners of the upper level.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.237
Now we have 8 of 11 cells per side.